		(uuid "e880c57a-3bd7-59f7-975d-e169fb6c0fae")
	)
	(text_box "OVP_TRIP high (08 comparator, 2,160 V) turns Q1111 on; 3V3_SUP drives about 8 mA through each LED (separate 240 ohm resistors, so one open LED does not disable the other). Each\nDarlington (collector HV_RTN, emitter STKx_G, VCEO 300 V) sinks >= 35 mA, which overpowers its running pump (short-circuit current about 10-15 mA [SIM]) and pulls the gate to\nabout -0.4..-1 V: both stacks conduct even while both controllers keep clocking. Default: OVP_TRIP pulled down 100 k here (contract §5.4) -> no LED current -> no force. 3V3_SUP is\nused on this sheet for these LEDs only (contract §4)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 248.901 0)
		(size 203.24 10.636)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
